        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: تعقیب کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تعقیب کردن (ta'qib kardan) — \"to chase, to pursue\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پلیس ماشین دزد را تعقیب کرد. Polis mâshin-e dozd râ ta'qib kard. The police chased the thief's car."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present ta'qib mikonad. In legal Persian also \"to prosecute\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ta'qib is borrowed from Arabic ta'qīb (EtymDB lists the Arabic word), usually glossed \"a following after\". kardan \"to do\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
